<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="circe_imu">

    <!--
      CIRCE IMU frame, parented to chassis_link.

      This replaces roverrobotics_description's accessories/imu.urdf, which parents
      imu_link to payload_link. CIRCE removed the payload deck, and that file is
      included by 16 other robot models in the upstream package, so it cannot be
      repointed without breaking all of them.

      An IMU wants to be rigidly fixed to the chassis anyway, not to a removable
      deck, so chassis_link is the better parent regardless.

      frame_id "imu_link" matches circe_bringup/config/bno055.yaml, which is NOT
      launched by default (no BNO055 is fitted). Nothing currently publishes on
      imu_link; see the imu0 note in circe_nav/config/localization_ekf.yaml.
      If CIRCE ends up using the D456's internal IMU instead of an external BNO055,
      that data arrives on camera_* frames and this link becomes unused.
    -->

    <link name="imu_link"/>

    <joint name="imu_to_chassis" type="fixed">
        <parent link="chassis_link"/>
        <child link="imu_link"/>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <!--
      Simulated IMU. Sim only - see the sim_mode note in circe_rover.urdf.xacro.

      Worth knowing: on hardware imu/data is synthesised by circe_perception/imu_fusion.py
      from the D456's raw 6-axis IMU (no BNO055 is fitted), so its yaw is unreferenced and
      its gyro bias is learned only after the rover has stood still. This sensor has
      neither limitation, so sim heading will be better behaved than the real robot's.
      See the divergence note in circe_gazebo/config/gz_bridge.yaml.

      *** update_rate 100 MATCHES THE HARDWARE /imu/data RATE. KEEP THEM EQUAL. ***
      imu_fusion.py is capped at publish_rate_limit 100.0 (circe_bringup/config/
      imu_d456.yaml), so that is what the EKF's imu0 receives on the robot. This was 50,
      which halved the EKF's IMU input in sim relative to hardware and made one health
      threshold impossible to share: circe_diagnostics checks /imu/data against a single
      floor in both environments (config/health_monitor.yaml, imu_fused).

      The Imu system that drives this used to be declared below, inside the model. It
      is world-scoped in Harmonic and now lives in circe_gazebo/worlds/*.sdf.
    -->
    <xacro:arg name="sim_mode" default="false" />
    <xacro:if value="$(arg sim_mode)">
    <gazebo reference="imu_link">
        <sensor name="imu" type="imu">
            <always_on>1</always_on>
            <update_rate>100</update_rate>
            <visualize>true</visualize>
            <topic>imu/data</topic>
            <enable_metrics>true</enable_metrics>
            <!-- gz_frame_id: ignition_frame_id is the Fortress spelling. -->
            <gz_frame_id>imu_link</gz_frame_id>
        </sensor>
    </gazebo>
    </xacro:if>

</robot>
